oth sides:\n\n\\[\n3x - 2x - 9 = 74\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx - 9 = 74\n\\]\n\n5. Add 9 to both sides to solve for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\nx = 74 + 9\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx = 83\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this solution using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the value of x\nx = 83\n\n# Calculate the left-hand side (LHS) and right-hand side (RHS) of the equation\nLHS = (3 * x - 9) / 2\nRHS = x + 37\n\n# Verify if LHS equals RHS\nprint((LHS, RHS, LHS == RHS))\n```\n```output\n(120.0, 120, True)\n```\nThe calculations confirm that the left-hand side (LHS) and right-hand side (RHS) of the equation are equal when \\( x = 83 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{LHS} = \\frac{3 \\cdot 83 - 9}{2} = 120.0\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{RHS} = 83 + 37 = 120\n\\]\n\nSince both sides are equal, the value of \\( x \\) is indeed correct.\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{83}\n\\]", 'To solve the problem, we need to translate the given statement into a mathematical equation and then solve for \\(x\\).\n\nThe statement "Half the value of \\(3x - 9\\) is \\(x + 37\\)" can be written as:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2}(3x - 9) = x + 37\n\\]\n\nWe can solve this equation step by step:\n\n1. Multiply both sides by 2 to eliminate the fraction:\n\\[\n3x - 9 = 2(x + 37)\n\\]\n\n2. Distribute the 2 on the right side:\n\\[\n3x - 9 = 2x + 74\n\\]\n\n3. Subtract \\(2x\\) from both sides to isolate \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx - 9 = 74\n\\]\n\n4. Add 9 to both sides to solve for \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx = 83\n\\]\n\nLet\'s verify this solution using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\n\n# Define the variable\nx = symbols(\'x\')\n\n# Define the equation\nequation = Eq((3*x - 9)/2, x + 37)\n\n# Solve the equation\nsolution = solve(equation, x)\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\n[83]\n```\nThe value of \\(x\\) is \\(\\boxed{83}\\).', 'To solve the problem, we need to translate the given statement into an algebraic equation and then solve for \\( x \\).\n\nThe statement "Half the value of \\( 3x - 9 \\) is \\( x + 37 \