des of the equation by 2:\n\\[\n3x - 9 = 2(x + 37)\n\\]\n\nNext, we'll distribute the 2 on the right side:\n\\[\n3x - 9 = 2x + 74\n\\]\n\nThen, we'll isolate \\( x \\) by subtracting \\( 2x \\) from both sides:\n\\[\n3x - 2x - 9 = 74\n\\]\n\\[\nx - 9 = 74\n\\]\n\nFinally, we'll add 9 to both sides to solve for \\( x \\):\n\\[\nx = 74 + 9\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 83\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this solution by substituting \\( x = 83 \\) back into the original equation to ensure it holds true. We'll use Python to confirm the result.\n```python\n# Define the value of x\nx = 83\n\n# Calculate the left side of the equation: (3x - 9) / 2\nleft_side = (3 * x - 9) / 2\n\n# Calculate the right side of the equation: x + 37\nright_side = x + 37\n\n# Check if both sides are equal\nprint((left_side, right_side, left_side == right_side))\n```\n```output\n(120.0, 120, True)\n```\nThe calculations confirm that when \\( x = 83 \\), both sides of the equation are equal. Therefore, the value of \\( x \\) is indeed \\(\\boxed{83}\\).", 'To solve the problem, we need to translate the given statement into an algebraic equation and then solve for \\(x\\). The statement "Half the value of \\(3x - 9\\) is \\(x + 37\\)" can be written as:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2}(3x - 9) = x + 37\n\\]\n\nLet\'s solve this step-by-step.\n\n1. First, we\'ll eliminate the fraction by multiplying both sides of the equation by 2:\n\n\\[\n3x - 9 = 2(x + 37)\n\\]\n\n2. Next, we\'ll distribute the 2 on the right side of the equation:\n\n\\[\n3x - 9 = 2x + 74\n\\]\n\n3. Now, we\'ll isolate \\(x\\) by subtracting \\(2x\\) from both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[\n3x - 2x - 9 = 74\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\nx - 9 = 74\n\\]\n\n4. Finally, we\'ll add 9 to both sides of the equation to solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\nx = 74 + 9\n\\]\n\nSo:\n\n\\[\nx = 83\n\\]\n\nLet\'s verify this solution by substituting \\(x = 83\\) back into the original equation to ensure it holds true. We\'ll use Python to confirm our result.\n```python\n# Define the