Solving the first equation for \\(q\\):\n\n\\[\n-48 - 9p + 3q = 0 \\implies q = 16 + 3p\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(q = 16 + 3p\\) into the second equation:\n\n\\[\n148 - p - 4(16 + 3p) = 0 \\implies 148 - p - 64 - 12p = 0 \\implies 84 - 13p = 0 \\implies p = \\frac{84}{13}\n\\]\n\nThen, substituting \\(p = \\frac{84}{13}\\) into \\(q = 16 + 3p\\):\n\n\\[\nq = 16 + 3 \\left( \\frac{84}{13} \\right) = 16 + \\frac{252}{13} = \\frac{208}{13} + \\frac{252}{13} = \\frac{460}{13}\n\\]\n\nFinally, substituting \\(p = \\frac{84}{13}\\) and \\(q = \\frac{460}{13}\\) into the third equation:\n\n\\[\n-44 + 4 \\left( \\frac{84}{13} \\right) + \\frac{460}{13} + r = 0 \\implies -44 + \\frac{336}{13} + \\frac{460}{13} + r = 0 \\implies -44 + \\frac{796}{13} + r = 0 \\implies r = 44 - \\frac{796}{13} = \\frac{572}{13} - \\frac{796}{13} = -\\frac{224}{13}\n\\]\n\nSo the ordered triple \\((p, q, r)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{84}{13}, \\frac{460}{13}, -\\frac{224}{13} \\right)\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, solve\n\n# Define the variables\np, q, r = symbols('p q r')\n\n# Define the equations based on the coefficients\neq1 = -48 - 9*p + 3*q\neq2 = 148 - p - 4*q\neq3 = -44 + 4*p + q + r\n\n# Solve the system of equations\nsolution = solve((eq1, eq2, eq3), (p, q, r))\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\n{p: 84/13, q: 460/13, r: -224/13}\n```\nThe solution to the system of equations confirms our previous calculations. The ordered triple \\((p, q, r)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\left( \\frac{84}{13}, \\frac{460}{13}, -\\frac{224}{13} \\right)}\n\\]", "To solve this problem, we need to find the values of \\(p\\), \\(q\\), and \\(r\\) such that the polynomial \\(x^3 - 3x^2 + 4x - 1\\) is a factor of \\(x^9 + px^6 + qx^3 + r\\).\n\nLet's denote the polynomial \\(x^3 - 3x^2 + 4x - 1\\) by \\(f(x)\\). If \\(f(x)\\) is a factor of \\(x^9 + px^6 + qx^3 + r\\), then the roots of \\(f(x)\\) must also be roots of \\(x^9 + px^6 + qx^3 + 