ues for \\( z + \\frac{1}{z} + z^2 + \\frac{1}{z^2} \\) for each of the fifth roots of unity (excluding 1) are all approximately \\(-1\\). The small numerical differences from \\(-1\\) are due to floating-point precision errors in the computation.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{-1}\\).", 'To solve the problem of subtracting \\(18_9\\) from \\(58_9\\) and expressing the answer in base 9, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the base 9 numbers to base 10.\n2. Perform the subtraction in base 10.\n3. Convert the result back to base 9.\n\nLet\'s start by converting \\(58_9\\) and \\(18_9\\) to base 10. The number \\(58_9\\) in base 10 is \\(5 \\cdot 9^1 + 8 \\cdot 9^0 = 5 \\cdot 9 + 8 \\cdot 1 = 45 + 8 = 53\\). The number \\(18_9\\) in base 10 is \\(1 \\cdot 9^1 + 8 \\cdot 9^0 = 1 \\cdot 9 + 8 \\cdot 1 = 9 + 8 = 17\\).\n\nNow we perform the subtraction in base 10: \\(53 - 17 = 36\\).\n\nNext, we convert the result \\(36_{10}\\) back to base 9. To do this, we repeatedly divide the number by 9 and keep track of the remainders.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&36 \\div 9 = 4 \\text{ remainder } 0 \\\\\n&4 \\div 9 = 0 \\text{ remainder } 4 \\\\\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \\(40_9\\). So, the final answer is \\(40_9\\).\n\nLet\'s verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Function to convert a base 10 number to base 9\r\ndef to_base_9(n):\r\n    if n == 0:\r\n        return "0"\r\n    digits = []\r\n    while n:\r\n        digits.append(int(n % 9))\r\n        n //= 9\r\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\r\n\r\n# Convert the base 9 numbers to base 10\r\nnum1_base_10 = 5 * 9 + 8\r\nnum2_base_10 = 1 * 9 + 8\r\n\r\n# Perform the subtraction in base 10\r\nresult_base_10 = num1_base_10 - num2_base_10\r\n\r\n# Convert the result back to base 9\r\nresult_base_9 = to_base_9(result_base_10)\r\nprint(result_base_9)\n```\n```output\n40\n```\nThe result of \\(58_9 - 18_9\\) in base 9 is \\(\\boxed{40_9}\\).', 'To solve the problem of subtracting \\(18_9\\) from \\(58_9\\) and expressing the answer in base 9, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the numbers from base 9 to base 10.\n2. Perform the subtraction in base 10.\n3. Convert the result back to base 9.\n\nLet\'s start by converting \\(58_9\\) and \\(18_9\\) to base 10.\n\nThe number \\(58_9\\) in base 10 is:\n\\[5 \\cdot 9^1 + 8 \\cdot 9^0 = 5 \\cdot 9 + 8 \\cdot 1 = 45 + 8 = 53_{10}.\\]\n\nThe number \\(18_9\\) in base 10 is:\n\\[1 \\cdot 9^1 + 8 \\cdot 9^0 = 1 \\cdot 9 + 8 \\cdot 1 = 9 + 8 = 17_{10}.\\]\n\nNow we perform the subtraction in base 10:\n\\[53_{10} - 17_{10} = 36_{10}.\\]\n\nNext, we need to convert \\(36_{10}\\) back to base 9. To do this, we repeatedly divide the number by 9 and keep track of the remainders.\n\n\\[36 \\div 9 = 4 \\text{ remainder } 0\\]\n\\[4 \\div 9 = 0 \\text{ remainder } 4\\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \\(40_9\\).\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\\[58_9 - 18_9 = 40_9.\\]\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Function to convert a base 10 number to base 9\ndef to_base_9(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % 9))\n        n //= 9\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert the base 9 numbers to base 10\nnum1_base_10 = 5 * 9 + 8\nnum2_base_10 = 1 * 9 + 8\n\n# Perform the subtraction in base 10\nresult_base_10 = num1_base_10 - num2_base_10\n\n# Convert the result back to base 9\nresult_base_9 = to_base_9(result_base_10)\nprint(result_base_9)\n```\n```output\n40\n```\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{40_9}\n\\]', 'To compute \\(58_9 - 18_9\\) and express the answer in base 9, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the base 9 numbers to base 10.\n2. Perform the subtraction in base 10.\n3. Convert the result back to base 9.\n\nLet\'s start by converting \\(58_9\\) and \\(18_9\\) to base 10. The general formula to convert a number from base \\(b\\) to base 10 is:\n\n\\[ \\text{number}_{10} = d_n \\cdot b^n + d_{n-1} \\cdot b^{n-1} + \\ldots + d_1 \\cdot b^1 + d_0 \\cdot b^0 \\]\n\nFor \\(58_9\\):\n\\[ 58_9 = 5 \\cdot 9^1 + 8 \\cdot 9^0 = 5 \\cdot 9 + 8 \\cdot 1 = 45 + 8 = 53_{10} \\]\n\nFor \\(18_9\\):\n\\[ 18_9 = 1 \\cdot 9^1 + 8 \\cdot 9^0 = 1 \\cdot 9 + 8 \\cdot 1 = 9 + 8 = 17_{10} \\]\n\nNow, we perform the subtraction in base 10:\n\\[ 53_{10} - 17_{10} = 36_{10} \\]\n\nNext, we convert \\(36_{10}\\) back to base 9. To convert a number from base 10 to base \\(b\\), we repeatedly divide the number by \\(b\\) and keep track of the remainders.\n\n\\[ 36 \\div 9 = 4 \\text{ remainder } 0 \\]\n\\[ 4 \\div 9 = 0 \\text{ remainder } 4 \\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \\(40_9\\). So, the final answer is:\n\\[ 58_9 - 18_9 = 40_9 \\]\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Function to convert a base 10 number to base 9\r\ndef to_base_9(n):\r\n    if n == 0:\r\n        return "0"\r\n    digits = []\r\n    while n:\r\n        digits.append(int(n % 9))\r\n        n //= 9\r\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\r\n\r\n# Convert 58_9 and 18_9 to base 10\r\nnum1_base_10 = 5 * 9 + 8\r\nnum2_base_10 = 1 * 9 + 8\r\n\r\n# Perform the subtraction in base 10\r\nresult_base_10 = num1_base_10 - num2_base_10\r\n\r\n# Convert the result back to base 9\r\nresult_base_9 = to_base_9(result_base_10)\r\nprint(result_base_9)\n```\n```output\n40\n```\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{40_9}\\).', 'To solve the problem of subtracting \\(18_9\\) from \\(58_9\\) in base 9, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert both numbers from base 9 to base 10.\n2. Perform the subtraction in base 10.\n3. Convert the result back to base 9.\n\nLet\'s start by converting \\(58_9\\) and \\(18_9\\) to base 10.\n\nThe number \\(58_9\\) in base 10 is:\n\\[5 \\cdot 9^1 + 8 \\cdot 9^0 = 5 \\cdot 9 + 8 \\cdot 1 = 45 + 8 = 53_{10}.\\]\n\nThe number \\(18_9\\) in base 10 is:\n\\[1 \\cdot 9^1 + 8 \\cdot 9^0 = 1 