 the given projection to solve for \\( y \\).\n\nLet's start by calculating the dot products and solving for \\( y \\) using Python.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable y\ny = sp.symbols('y')\n\n# Define the vectors a and b\na = sp.Matrix([2, y, -5])\nb = sp.Matrix([1, -2, 1])\n\n# Compute the dot products\ndot_product_ab = a.dot(b)\ndot_product_bb = b.dot(b)\n\n# Compute the projection\nprojection = (dot_product_ab / dot_product_bb) * b\n\n# Given projection\ngiven_projection = (5/6) * b\n\n# Solve for y\nequation = sp.Eq(projection, given_projection)\nsolution = sp.solve(equation, y)\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\n{y: -1.00000000000000}\n```\nThe value of \\( y \\) that satisfies the given projection condition is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-1}\n\\]", "To find the value of \\( y \\) such that the projection of \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ y \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}\\) onto \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is \\(\\frac{5}{6} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we need to use the formula for the projection of vector \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) onto vector \\(\\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ y \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe projection is:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{b} = \\frac{5}{6} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we need to calculate \\(\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 2 \\cdot 1 + y \\cdot (-2) + (-5) \\cdot 1 = 2 - 2y - 5 = -3 - 2y\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 1^2 + (-2)^2 + 1^2 = 1 + 4 + 1 = 6\n\\]\n\nSo, the projection is:\n\\[\n\\frac{-3 - 2y}{6} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatri