b)\\) of integers such that \\(|a + bi| \\le 5\\) is \\(\\boxed{81}\\).", 'To solve this problem, we need to evaluate different possible placements of parentheses in the expression \\(1 + 2 + 3 - 4 + 5 + 6\\) and find the minimum value. We can do this by systematically evaluating all possible ways to add parentheses and then determining the minimum value obtained.\n\nHere\'s the plan:\n1. Generate all possible ways to add parentheses to the expression.\n2. Evaluate each expression to find its value.\n3. Determine the minimum value from these evaluations.\n\nWe\'ll use Python to automate this process. Let\'s start by writing a function to evaluate the expression with different placements of parentheses and then find the minimum value.\n```python\nfrom itertools import combinations\n\ndef evaluate_expression(expr):\n    # This function evaluates the expression with given parentheses\n    try:\n        return eval(expr)\n    except (SyntaxError, ValueError):\n        return float(\'inf\')  # Return a large value if the expression is invalid\n\ndef generate_parentheses(expr):\n    # Generate all possible ways to add parentheses\n    n = len(expr)\n    min_value = float(\'inf\')\n    best_expr = ""\n    \n    # Iterate over all possible positions to add parentheses\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i+1, n+1):\n            left_expr = expr[:i]\n            right_expr = expr[i:j]\n            remaining_expr = expr[j:]\n            \n            # Try different placements of parentheses\n            for k in range(1, len(right_expr)):\n                left_paren_expr = f"({left_expr} + {right_expr[:k]} - {right_expr[k:]})"\n                right_paren_expr = f"({left_expr} - {right_expr[:k]} + {right_expr[k:]})"\n                if evaluate_expression(left_paren_expr + remaining_expr) < min_value:\n                    min_value = evaluate_expression(left_paren_expr + remaining_expr)\n                    best_expr = left_paren_expr + remaining_expr\n        