al answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{1}{137} + i}\n\\]", "To solve the problem, we need to analyze the function \\(F(z) = \\frac{z + i}{z - i}\\) and its iterations. We are given \\(z_0 = \\frac{1}{137} + i\\) and need to find \\(z_{2002}\\).\n\nFirst, let's compute the first few iterations of \\(F(z)\\) to see if there is a pattern:\n\n1. \\(z_1 = F(z_0) = F\\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right) = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right) + i}{\\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right) - i} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + 2i}{\\frac{1}{137}} = 1 + 274i\\).\n\n2. \\(z_2 = F(z_1) = F(1 + 274i) = \\frac{(1 + 274i) + i}{(1 + 274i) - i} = \\frac{1 + 275i}{1 + 273i} = \\frac{(1 + 275i)(1 - 273i)}{(1 + 273i)(1 - 273i)} = \\frac{1 - 273i + 275i + 74525}{1 + 74529} = \\frac{74526 + 2i}{74530} = \\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i\\).\n\n3. \\(z_3 = F(z_2) = F\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i\\right) = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i\\right) + i}{\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i\\right) - i} = \\frac{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{37266}{37265}i}{\\frac{37263}{37265} - \\frac{37264}{37265}i} = \\frac{37263 + 37266i}{37263 - 37264i} = \\frac{(37263 + 37266i)(37263 + 37264i)}{(37263 - 37264i)(37263 + 37264i)} = \\frac{1388506969 + 1388506968i + 1388506968i - 1388506968}{1388506969 + 1388506968} = \\frac{1 + 274i}{1} = 1 + 274i\\).\n\nWe can see that \\(z_3 = z_1\\), and since \\(z_2 = F(z_1)\\), we can infer that \\(z_4 = F(z_3) = F(z_1) = z_2\\), and so on. This indicates that the sequence is periodic with a period of 2. Therefore, \\(z_{2002} = z_2\\).\n\nLet's confirm this by calculating \\(z_2\\) using the function \\(F(z)\\):\n\n\\[z_2 = F(z_1) = F(1 + 274i) = \\frac{(1 + 274i) + i}{(1 + 274i) - i} = \\frac{1 + 275i}{1 + 273i} = \\frac{(1 + 275i)(1 - 273i)}{(1 + 273i)(1 - 273i)} = \\frac{1 - 273i + 275i + 74525}{1 + 74529} = \\frac{74526 + 2i}{74530} = \\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i.\\]\n\nThus, \\(z_{2002} = z_2 = \\frac{3726