f two vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1 \\end{vmatrix}\n= \\mathbf{i}(2 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-2)) - \\mathbf{j}(1 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-3)) + \\mathbf{k}(1 \\cdot (-2) - 2 \\cdot (-3))\n= \\mathbf{i}(2 + 6) - \\mathbf{j}(1 + 9) + \\mathbf{k}(-2 + 6)\n= \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe magnitude of this cross product is:\n\n\\[\n\\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\| = \\sqrt{8^2 + (-10)^2 + 4^2} = \\sqrt{64 + 100 + 16} = \\sqrt{180} = 6\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of triangle \\(OAB\\) is half of this magnitude:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\| = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 6\\sqrt{5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Define the vectors OA and OB\nOA = np.array([1, 2, 3])\nOB = np.array([-3, -2, 1])\n\n# Compute the cross product of OA and OB\ncross_product = np.cross(OA, OB)\n\n# Compute the magnitude of the cross product\nmagnitude = np.linalg.norm(cross_product)\n\n# The area of the triangle is half the magnitude of the cross product\narea = 0.5 * magnitude\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n6.708203932499369\n```\nThe computed area of triangle \\(OAB\\) is approximately \\(6.708\\), which is equal to \\(3\\sqrt{5}\\) when expressed in exact form. Therefore, the area of triangle \\(OAB\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{3\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]", "The area of triangle $OAB$ can be found using the cross product of vectors $\\overrightarrow{OA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB}$. The area of the triangle is half the magnitude of the cross product of these two vectors.\n\nFirst, let's compute the cross product $\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}$. The cross product of two vectors $\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} a_1 \\\\ a_2 \\\\ a_3 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} b_1 \\\\ b_2 \\\\ b_3 \\end{pmatrix}$ is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} a_2 b_3 - a_3 b_2 \\\\ a_3 b_1 - a_1 b_3 \\\\ a_1 b_2 - a_2 b_1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFor $\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$, the cross product is:\n\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-2) \\\\ 3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1 \\\\ 1 \\cdot (-2) - 2 \\cdot (-3) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 + 6 \\\\ -9 - 1 \\\\ -2 + 6 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe magnitude of this cross product vector is:\n\n\\[\n\\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\| = \\sqrt{8^2 + (-10)^2 + 4^2} = \\sqrt{64 + 100 + 16} = \\sqrt{180} = 6\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nThe area of triangle $OAB$ is half of this magnitude:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6\\sqrt{5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Define the vectors OA and OB\nOA = np.array([1, 2, 3])\nOB = np.array([-3, -2, 1])\n\n# Compute the cross product of OA and OB\ncross_product = np.cross(OA, OB)\n\n# Compute the magnitude of the cross product\nmagnitude = np.linalg.norm(cross_product)\n\n# The area of the triangle is half the magnitude of the cross product\narea = 0.5 * magnitude\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n6.708203932499369\n```\nThe computed area of the triangle $OAB$ is approximately $6.708$, which is equal to $3\\sqrt{5}$. Therefore, the exact area of the triangle $OAB$ is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{3\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]", "To find the area of triangle \\(OAB\\) with given points \\(O\\), \\(A\\), and \\(B\\), we can use the following steps:\n\n1. Determine the vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{OA}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB}\\).\n2. Compute the cross product of \\(\\overrightarrow{OA}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB}\\).\n3. Find the magnitude of the cross product.\n4. The area of the triangle \\(OAB\\) is half the magnitude of the cross product.\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe cross product \\(\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\) is calculated as follows:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1 \\end{vmatrix} = \\mathbf{i}(2 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-2)) - \\mathbf{j}(1 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-3)) + \\mathbf{k}(1 \\cdot (-2) - 2 \\cdot (-3))\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\mathbf{i}(2 + 6) - \\mathbf{j}(1 + 9) + \\mathbf{k}(-2 + 6) = 8\\mathbf{i} - 10\\mathbf{j} + 4\\mathbf{k} = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe magnitude of the cross product is:\n\\[\n\\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\| = \\sqrt{8^2 + (-10)^2 + 4^2} = \\sqrt{64 + 100 + 16} = \\sqrt{180} = 6\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nThe area of triangle \\(OAB\\) is half of this magnitude:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 6\\sqrt{5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Define the vectors OA and OB\nOA = np.array([1, 2, 3])\nOB = np.array([-3, -2, 1])\n\n# Compute the cross product of OA and OB\ncross_product = np.cross(OA, OB)\n\n# Compute the magnitude of the cross product\nmagnitude = np.linalg.norm(cross_product)\n\n# The area of the triangle OAB is half the magnitude of the cross product\narea = 0.5 * magnitude\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n6.708203932499369\n```\nThe area of triangle \\(OAB\\) is \\(3\\sqrt{5}\\), which is approximately 6.708. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{3\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]", "To find the area of the triangle \\(OA