(y_2 \\cdot 1 - y_3 \\cdot 1) - y_1(x_2 \\cdot 1 - x_3 \\cdot 1) + 1(x_2 y_3 - x_3 y_2) = x_1(y_2 - y_3) - y_1(x_2 - x_3) + (x_2 y_3 - x_3 y_2).\n\\]\n\nLet's denote the determinant by \\(D\\). Then we need to find \\(D^2\\). We can use the given conditions to find the value of \\(D\\).\n\nThe given conditions are:\n\\[\n(x_1 - x_2)^2 + (y_1 - y_2)^2 = 9,\n\\]\n\\[\n(x_1 - x_3)^2 + (y_1 - y_3)^2 = 16,\n\\]\n\\[\n(x_2 - x_3)^2 + (y_2 - y_3)^2 = 25.\n\\]\n\nThese conditions imply that the points \\((x_1, y_1)\\), \\((x_2, y_2)\\), and \\((x_3, y_3)\\) form a right triangle with sides of lengths 3, 4, and 5. The area of this triangle can be calculated using the formula for the area of a right triangle, which is \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 3 \\times 4 = 6\\).\n\nThe area of the triangle can also be expressed in terms of the determinant \\(D\\). The area of the triangle formed by the points \\((x_1, y_1)\\), \\((x_2, y_2)\\), and \\((x_3, y_3)\\) is given by \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\left| D \\right|\\). Therefore, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2} \\left| D \\right| = 6 \\implies \\left| D \\right| = 12.\n\\]\n\nThus, \\(D^2 = 12^2 = 144\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given conditions\r\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\r\n\r\n# Define the variables\r\nx1, y1, x2, y2, x3, y3 = symbols('x1 y1 x2 y2 x3 y3')\r\n\r\n# Define the equations based on the given conditions\r\neq1 = Eq((x1 - x2)**2 + (y1 - y2)**2, 9)\r\neq2 = Eq((x1 - x3)**2 + (y1 - y3)**2, 16)\r\neq3 = Eq((x2 - x3)**2 + (y2 - y3)**2, 25)\r\n\r\n# Solve the system of equations\r\nsolutions = solve((eq1, eq2, eq3), (x1, y1, x2, y2, x3, y3), dict=True)\r\n\r\n# Calculate the determinant for each solution\r\ndet_values = []\r\nfor sol in solutions:\r\n    x1_val = sol[x1]\r\n    y1_val = sol[y1]\r\n    x2_val = sol[x2]\r\n    y2_val = sol[y2]\r\n    x3_val = sol[x3]\r\n    y3_val = sol[y3]\r\n    determinant = x1_val * (y2_val - y3_val) - y1_val