minator, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by \\(\\sqrt{3}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n\\]\n\nSo the final answer is \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the expression\nexpr = sp.sqrt(sp.root(sp.sqrt(1/729), 3))\n\n# Simplify the expression\nsimplified_expr = sp.simplify(expr)\n\n# Rationalize the denominator\nrationalized_expr = sp.together(simplified_expr)\n\nprint(rationalized_expr)\n```\n```output\n0.577350269189626\n```\nThe numerical value of \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\) is approximately \\(0.577350269189626\\), which matches the result from the code.\n\nTherefore, the simplified expression with a rational denominator is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\n\\]", "To solve the expression \\(\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}\\), we can break it down step by step.\n\n1. Start with the innermost expression: \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}\\).\n2. Then, take the cube root of the result.\n3. Finally, take the square root of the result from step 2.\n\nLet's solve this step by step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n\nFirst, we need to calculate \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}\\). The square root of \\(\\frac{1}{729}\\) is \\(\\frac{1}{27}\\) because \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{1}}{\\sqrt{729}} = \\frac{1}{27}\\).\n\nNext, we need to calculate \\(\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{1}{27}}\\). The cube root of \\(\\frac{1}{27}\\) is \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) because \\(\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{1}{27}} = \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{1}}{\\sqrt[3]{27}} = \\frac{1}{3}\\).\n\nFinally, we need to calculate \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}}\\). The square root of \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) is \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{1}}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\).\n\nTo rationalize the denominator, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by \\(\\sqrt{3}\\), which gives us \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the