 and then evaluate it at \\(x=4\\).\n\nLet's break it down step by step:\n\n1. Simplify the expression \\((3x-2)(4x+1)-(3x-2)4x+1\\).\n2. Substitute \\(x=4\\) into the simplified expression.\n3. Evaluate the expression to get the final answer.\n\nLet's start with the simplification:\n\n\\[\n(3x-2)(4x+1)-(3x-2)4x+1\n\\]\n\nFirst, expand \\((3x-2)(4x+1)\\):\n\n\\[\n(3x-2)(4x+1) = 3x \\cdot 4x + 3x \\cdot 1 - 2 \\cdot 4x - 2 \\cdot 1 = 12x^2 + 3x - 8x - 2 = 12x^2 - 5x - 2\n\\]\n\nNow substitute this back into the original expression:\n\n\\[\n12x^2 - 5x - 2 - (3x-2)4x + 1\n\\]\n\nSimplify \\((3x-2)4x\\):\n\n\\[\n(3x-2)4x = 3x \\cdot 4x - 2 \\cdot 4x = 12x^2 - 8x\n\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n12x^2 - 5x - 2 - (12x^2 - 8x) + 1 = 12x^2 - 5x - 2 - 12x^2 + 8x + 1 = 3x - 1\n\\]\n\nNow we need to evaluate the expression \\(3x - 1\\) at \\(x=4\\):\n\n\\[\n3(4) - 1 = 12 - 1 = 11\n\\]\n\nSo the value of the expression when \\(x=4\\) is \\(11\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the expression as a function\ndef expression_value(x):\n    return (3 * x - 2) * (4 * x + 1) - (3 * x - 2) * 4 * x + 1\n\n# Evaluate the expression at x = 4\nx = 4\nresult = expression_value(x)\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n11\n```\nThe value of the expression \\((3x-2)(4x+1)-(3x-2)4x+1\\) when \\(x=4\\) is \\(\\boxed{11}\\).", "To solve the expression \\((3x-2)(4x+1)-(3x-2)4x+1\\) when \\(x=4\\), we can break it down into smaller parts and evaluate it step by step.\n\n1. First, let's simplify the expression \\((3x-2)(4x+1)-(3x-2)4x+1\\).\n2. Then we will substitute \\(x=4\\) into the simplified expression.\n3. Finally, we will evaluate the expression to get the result.\n\nLet's start by simplifying the expression:\n\n\\[\n(3x-2)(4x+1)-(3x-2)4x+1\n\\]\n\nWe can factor out \\((3x-2)\\) from the first two terms:\n\n\\[\n(3x-2)(4x+1-4x) + 1 = (3x-2)(1) + 1 = 3x - 2 + 1 = 3x - 1\n\\]\n\nNow we substitute \\(x=4\\) into the simplified expression \\(3x - 1\\):\n\n\\[\n3