\n\nx = math.log10(rhs)\nprint(x)\n```\n```output\n4.0\n```\nThe solution to the equation \\(10^x - 10 = 9990\\) is \\(x = 4\\).\n\nThus, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).", "To solve the equation \\(10^x - 10 = 9990\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Add 10 to both sides of the equation to isolate the term with \\(x\\):\n   \\[\n   10^x = 10000\n   \\]\n2. Express 10000 as a power of 10:\n   \\[\n   10^x = 10^4\n   \\]\n3. Since the bases are the same, we can equate the exponents:\n   \\[\n   x = 4\n   \\]\n\nLet's verify this solution using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the equation and solve for x\r\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\r\n\r\n# Define the variable\r\nx = symbols('x')\r\n\r\n# Define the equation\r\nequation = Eq(10**x - 10, 9990)\r\n\r\n# Solve the equation\r\nsolution = solve(equation, x)\r\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\n[4]\n```\nThe solution to the equation \\(10^x - 10 = 9990\\) is \\(x = 4\\).\n\nThus, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).", "To solve the equation \\(10^x - 10 = 9990\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Add 10 to both sides of the equation to isolate the term with the exponent:\n   \\[\n   10^x = 10000\n   \\]\n2. Express 10000 as a power of 10:\n   \\[\n   10^x = 10^4\n   \\]\n3. Since the bases are the same, we can equate the exponents:\n   \\[\n   x = 4\n   \\]\n\nLet's verify this solution using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the equation and solve for x\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\n\n# Define the variable\nx = symbols('x')\n\n# Define the equation\nequation = Eq(10**x - 10, 9990)\n\n# Solve the equation\nsolution = solve(equation, x)\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\n[4]\n```\nThe solution to the equation \\(10^x - 10 = 9990\\) is \\(x = 4\\).\n\nThus, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).", "To solve the equation \\(10^x - 10 = 9990\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Add 10 to both sides of the equation to isolate \\(10^x\\):\n   \\[\n   10^x = 10000\n   \\]