\]\n   so \\(r = \\frac{7}{2}\\) is not a valid solution because it would make the denominator zero.\n\nTherefore, the only valid solution is \\(r = 4\\).\n\nLet's verify this using Python code to ensure the accuracy of the result.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\r\n\r\n# Define the variable\r\nr = symbols('r')\r\n\r\n# Define the equation\r\nequation = Eq((6*r**2 - 19*r - 7) / (2*r - 7), 4*r - 3)\r\n\r\n# Solve the equation\r\nsolutions = solve(equation, r)\r\nprint(solutions)\n```\n```output\n[4]\n```\nThe solution to the equation \\(\\frac{6r^2 - 19r - 7}{2r - 7} = 4r - 3\\) is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).", "To solve for \\( r \\) in the equation \\(\\frac{6r^2 - 19r - 7}{2r - 7} = 4r - 3\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. First, we'll eliminate the denominator by multiplying both sides of the equation by \\(2r - 7\\).\n2. This will give us a simpler polynomial equation.\n3. Then, we'll solve the resulting equation for \\(r\\).\n\nLet's start by performing the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{6r^2 - 19r - 7}{2r - 7} \\cdot (2r - 7) = (4r - 3) \\cdot (2r - 7)\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n6r^2 - 19r - 7 = (4r - 3)(2r - 7)\n\\]\n\nNext, we'll expand the right-hand side:\n\n\\[\n6r^2 - 19r - 7 = 4r \\cdot 2r + 4r \\cdot (-7) + (-3) \\cdot 2r + (-3) \\cdot (-7)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n6r^2 - 19r - 7 = 8r^2 - 28r - 6r + 21\n\\]\n\n\\[\n6r^2 - 19r - 7 = 8r^2 - 34r + 21\n\\]\n\nNow, we'll move all terms to one side of the equation to set it to zero:\n\n\\[\n6r^2 - 19r - 7 - 8r^2 + 34r - 21 = 0\n\\]\n\n\\[\n-2r^2 + 15r - 28 = 0\n\\]\n\nThis is a standard quadratic equation. We can solve it using the quadratic formula \\(r = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\), where \\(a = -2\\), \\(b = 15\\), and \\(c = -28\\).\n\nLet's calculate the discriminant first:\n\n\\[\nb^2 - 4ac = 15^2 - 4(-2)(-28) = 225 - 224 = 1\n\\]\n\nNow, we can find the solutions for \\(r\\):\n\n\\[\nr = \\frac{-15 \\pm \\sqrt{1}}{2(-2)} = \\frac{-15 \\pm 1}{-4}\n\\]\n\nThis gives us two solutions: