120691 + 1.457055i. \\]\n\nThese roots are the vertices of a convex polygon in the complex plane. To find the area of this polygon, we can use the Shoelace formula (also known as Gauss's area formula for polygons). For a polygon with vertices \\((x_1, y_1), (x_2, y_2), \\ldots, (x_n, y_n)\\), the area \\(A\\) is given by:\n\\[ A = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} (x_i y_{i+1} - y_i x_{i+1}) + (x_n y_1 - y_n x_1) \\right|. \\]\n\nLet's use this formula to calculate the area of the polygon formed by the roots. We will first extract the real and imaginary parts of the roots, then apply the Shoelace formula.\n```python\n# Extract real and imaginary parts of the roots\nx = np.real(roots)\ny = np.imag(roots)\n\n# Apply the Shoelace formula to calculate the area of the polygon\nn = len(x)\narea = 0.5 * np.abs(np.dot(x, np.roll(y, 1)) - np.dot(y, np.roll(x, 1)))\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\nNameError: name 'np' is not defined\n```\nIt seems there was an issue with the execution environment. Let me re-run the calculation of the area using the Shoelace formula manually.\n\nThe vertices of the polygon are approximately:\n\\[ (1.18365996, -1.37472964), \\]\n\\[ (-1.18365996, 1.37472964), \\]\n\\[ (-0.36120691, -1.457055), \\]\n\\[ (0.36120691, 1.457055). \\]\n\nUsing the Shoelace formula:\n\\[ A = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 1.18365996 \\cdot 1.37472964 + (-1.18365996) \\cdot (-1.457055) + (-0.36120691) \\cdot 1.457055 + 0.36120691 \\cdot (-1.37472964) - \\left( -1.37472964 \\cdot (-1.18365996) + 1.37472964 \\cdot (-0.36120691) + (-1.457055) \\cdot 0.36120691 + 1.457055 \\cdot 1.18365996 \\right) \\right|. \\]\n\nLet's calculate this step by step.\n```python\n# Extract real and imaginary parts of the roots\r\nx = np.real(roots)\r\ny = np.imag(roots)\r\n\r\n# Apply the Shoelace formula to calculate the area of the polygon\r\nn = len(x)\r\narea = 0.5 * np.abs(np.dot(x, np.roll(y, 1)) - np.dot(y, np.roll(x, 1)))\r\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\nNameError: name 'np' is not defined\n