ectors:\n$$\\vec{u} = \\left(\n\\begin{array}{c}\n\\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n-\\frac{19}{2} \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right) \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\vec{v} = \\left(\n\\begin{array}{c}\n\\frac{13}{2} \\\\\n\\frac{11}{2} \\\\\n-3 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right)$$ The cross product of $\\vec{u}$ and $\\vec{v}$ can be calculated using the determinant of a matrix formed by the standard basis vectors and the components of the vectors. The result is a vector perpendicular to both $\\vec{u}$ and $\\vec{v}$:\n$$\\vec{u} \\times \\vec{v} = \\left|\n\\begin{array}{ccc}\n\\hat{i} & \\hat{j} & \\hat{k} \\\\\n\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{19}{2} \\\\\n\\frac{13}{2} & \\frac{11}{2} & -3 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right|$$\n\nExpanding the determinant, we get:\n$$\\vec{u} \\times \\vec{v} = \\left(\n\\begin{array}{c}\n\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)(-3) - \\left(-\\frac{19}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{11}{2}\\right) \\\\\n\\left(-\\frac{19}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{13}{2}\\right) - \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(-3\\right) \\\\\n\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{11}{2}\\right) - \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{13}{2}\\right) \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right)$$\n\nSimplifying each component:\n$$\\vec{u} \\times \\vec{v} = \\left(\n\\begin{array}{c}\n\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{209}{4} \\\\\n-\\frac{247}{4} + \\frac{3}{2} \\\\\n\\frac{11}{4} + \\frac{13}{4} \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right)$$\n$$\\vec{u} \\times \\vec{v} = \\left(\n\\begin{array}{c}\n\\frac{215}{4} \\\\\n-\\frac{241}{4} \\\\\n\\frac{24}{4} \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right)$$\n$$\\vec{u} \\times \\vec{v} = \\left(\n\\begin{array}{c}\n\\frac{215}{4} \\\\\n-\\frac{241}{4} \\\\\n6 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right)$$\n\nSo the cross product is:\n$$\\vec{u} \\times \\vec{v} = \\left(\n\\begin{array}{c}\n\\frac{215}{4} \\\\\n-\\frac{241}{4} \\\\\n6 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\right)$$\n\nHow", "To solve this problem, let's break it down step-by-step:\n\n1. Let \\( n \\) be the number of leaves in the book. Since each leaf has 2 p