nd equation to find \\(b\\):\n\n\\[\nb + (-8) = -3 \\implies b - 8 = -3 \\implies b = 5\n\\]\n\nFinally, we substitute the value of \\(b\\) into the first equation to find \\(a\\):\n\n\\[\na + 5 = 8 \\implies a = 3\n\\]\n\nNow we have \\(a = 3\\), \\(b = 5\\), and \\(c = -8\\). The product \\(abc\\) is:\n\n\\[\nabc = 3 \\cdot 5 \\cdot (-8) = -120\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure the result is accurate.\n```python\n# Given equations\n# a + b = 8\n# b + c = -3\n# a + c = -5\n\n# Solving for a, b, and c\na_plus_b = 8\nb_plus_c = -3\na_plus_c = -5\n\n# Sum of all three equations\nsum_all = a_plus_b + b_plus_c + a_plus_c\n\n# Since a + b + c = 0\na_plus_b_plus_c = sum_all // 2\n\n# Finding individual values\nc = a_plus_b_plus_c - a_plus_b\nb = b_plus_c - c\na = a_plus_b - b\n\n# Calculating the product abc\nabc = a * b * c\nprint(abc)\n```\n```output\n-120\n```\nThe value of the product \\(abc\\) is \\(\\boxed{-120}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to find the values of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) that satisfy the given equations. The equations are:\n\n1. \\(a + b = 8\\)\n2. \\(b + c = -3\\)\n3. \\(a + c = -5\\)\n\nWe can solve this system of equations step by step.\n\nFirst, we can add all three equations together:\n\n\\[\n(a + b) + (b + c) + (a + c) = 8 + (-3) + (-5)\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n2a + 2b + 2c = 0\n\\]\n\nDividing through by 2, we get:\n\n\\[\na + b + c = 0\n\\]\n\nNow we can use this equation to find the values of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\). We can substitute the value of \\(a + b\\) from the first equation into the equation \\(a + b + c = 0\\):\n\n\\[\n8 + c = 0 \\implies c = -8\n\\]\n\nNext, we can substitute the value of \\(c\\) into the second equation to find \\(b\\):\n\n\\[\nb + (-8) = -3 \\implies b = 5\n\\]\n\nFinally, we can substitute the value of \\(b\\) into the first equation to find \\(a\\):\n\n\\[\na + 5 = 8 \\implies a = 3\n\\]\n\nNow we have the values \\(a = 3\\), \\(b = 5\\), and \\(c = -8\\). The product \\(abc\\) is:\n\n\\[\nabc = 3 \\cdot 5 \\cdot (-8) = -120\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given equations\r\n# a + b = 8\r\n# b + c = -3\r\n# a + c = -5\r\n\r\n# Solving the equations\r\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\r\n\r\n# Define the variables\r\na, b, c = symbols('a b c')\r\n\r\n# Define the equations\r\neq1 = Eq(a + b, 8)\r\neq2 = Eq(b + c, -3)\r\neq3 = Eq(a + c, -5)\r\n\r\n# Solve the system of equations\r\nsolution = solve((eq1, eq2, eq3), (a, b, c))\r\n\r\n# Extract the values of a, b, and c\r\na_val = solution[a]\r\nb_val = solution[b]\r\nc_val = solution[c]\r\n\r\n# Calculate the product abc\r\nabc_product = a_val * b_val * c_val\r\nprint((a_val, b_val, c_val, abc_product))\n```\n```output\n(3, 5, -8, -120)\n```\nThe values of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) are \\(3\\), \\(5\\), and \\(-8\\) respectively. The product \\(abc\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-120}\n\\]", 'To find the value of the product \\(abc\\), we need to determine the values of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) from the given equations:\n\n1. \\(a + b = 8\\)\n2. \\(b + c = -3\\)\n3. \\(a + c = -5\\)\n\nWe can solve these equations step by step. First, we can add all three equations together:\n\n\\[\n(a + b) + (b + c) + (a + c) = 8 + (-3) + (-5)\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n2a + 2b + 2c = 0\n\\]\n\nDividing both sides by 2, we get:\n\n\\[\na + b + c = 0\n\\]\n\nNow we can use this equation to find the value of each variable. We can substitute the first equation \\(a + b = 8\\) into \\(a + b + c = 0\\) to find \\(c\\):\n\n\\[\n8 + c = 0 \\implies c = -8\n\\]\n\nNext, we can substitute \\(c = -8\\) into the second equation \\(b + c = -3\\) to find \\(b\\):\n\n\\[\nb - 8 = -3 \\implies b = 5\n\\]\n\nFinally, we can substitute \\(b = 5\\) into the first equation \\(a + b = 8\\) to find \\(a\\):\n\n\\[\na + 5 = 8 \\implies a = 3\n\\]\n\nNow that we have the values \\(a = 3\\), \\(b = 5\\), and \\(c = -8\\), we can find the product \\(abc\\):\