\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ) - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|^2 = \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(84^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nNext, we solve for \\(\\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\|\\):\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| = \\frac{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ) - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|^2}{\\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(84^\\circ)}\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the angle between \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\). We use the dot product:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(\\theta)\n\\]\n\nWe substitute the expression for \\(\\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\|\\):\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\left( \\frac{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ) - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|^2}{\\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(84^\\circ)} \\right) \\cos(\\theta)\n\\]\n\nSimplify:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 \\cos(29^\\circ) - \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(84^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nWe equate this to the dot product expression:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 \\cos(29^\\circ) - \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(84^\\circ) = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(\\theta)\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(\\cos(\\theta)\\):\n\\[\n\\cos(\\theta) = \\frac{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 \\cos(29^\\circ) - \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(84^\\circ)}{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\|}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we find \\(\\theta\\):\n\\[\n\\theta = \\arccos\\left( \\frac{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 \\cos(29^\\circ) - \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(84^\\circ)}{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\|} \\right)\n\\]\n\nLet's use Python to calculate this.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given angles in degrees\nangle_ab = 29\nangle_b_ab_minus_b = 84\n\n# Convert angles to radians\nangle_ab_rad = math.radians(angle_ab)\nangle_b_ab_minus_b_rad = math.radians(angl