ulate the remainder of 2004 divided by 12\nremainder = 2004 % 12\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nThe remainder when 2004 is divided by 12 is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).", 'To find the remainder of 2004 divided by 12, we can use the division algorithm. The division algorithm states that for any integers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) (with \\(b > 0\\)), there exist unique integers \\(q\\) (the quotient) and \\(r\\) (the remainder) such that:\n\n\\[a = bq + r\\]\nwhere \\(0 \\leq r < b\\).\n\nIn this problem, \\(a = 2004\\) and \\(b = 12\\). We need to find \\(q\\) and \\(r\\) such that:\n\n\\[2004 = 12q + r\\]\nwhere \\(0 \\leq r < 12\\).\n\nFirst, we perform the division of 2004 by 12 to find the quotient \\(q\\):\n\n\\[2004 \\div 12 = 167\\]\n\nSo, the quotient \\(q\\) is 167. Now, we can find the remainder \\(r\\) by substituting \\(q\\) back into the equation:\n\n\\[2004 = 12 \\times 167 + r\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(12 \\times 167\\):\n\n\\[12 \\times 167 = 2004\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\n\\[2004 = 2004 + r\\]\n\nSubtracting 2004 from both sides of the equation, we get:\n\n\\[r = 2004 - 2004 = 0\\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when 2004 is divided by 12 is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).', "To find the remainder of \\(2004^{2004}\\) divided by 12, we can use modular arithmetic. First, we need to simplify \\(2004 \\mod 12\\).\n\n1. Calculate \\(2004 \\mod 12\\):\n\\[ 2004 \\div 12 = 167 \\text{ with a remainder of } 0. \\]\nSo, \\(2004 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{12}\\).\n\n2. This means \\(2004^{2004} \\equiv 0^{2004} \\equiv 0 \\pmod{12}\\).\n\nTherefore, the remainder when \\(2004^{2004}\\) is divided by 12 is \\(0\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the remainder of 2004^2004 divided by 12\nremainder = pow(2004, 2004, 12)\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nThe remainder of \\(2004^{2004}\\) divided by 12 is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).", "To find the remainder of \\(2004^{2004}\\) divided by 12, we can use modular arithmetic properties. Specifically, we can simplify the problem by finding \\(2004 \\mod 12\\) first, and then raising the result to the power of 2004 and taking modulo 12 again.\n\n1. First, we find \\(2004 \\mod 12\\):\n\\[2004 \\div 12 = 167 \\text{ with a remainder of } 0.\\]\nSo, \\(2004 \\equiv 0 \\mod 12\\).\n\n2. Now, we need to find \\(0^{2004} \\mod 12\\):\n\\[0^{2004} = 0,\\]\nand\n\\[0 \\mod 12 = 0.\\]\n\nSo, the remainder of \\(2004^{2004}\\) divided by 12 is \\(0\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the remainder of 2004^2004 divided by 12\nremainder = pow(2004, 2004, 12)\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nThe remainder of \\(2004^{2004}\\) divided by 12 is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).", 'What is the remainder of 2004 divided by 13? \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\boxed{?} \\bo