n# Calculate u\nu = (b * inverse_a) % m\nprint(u)\n```\n```output\n41\n```\nThe smallest positive integer solution to the congruence \\(7u \\equiv 23 \\pmod{50}\\) is \\(u = 41\\). Since we simplified the original congruence by dividing by 2, we need to check if there are any other solutions in the range from 1 to 100.\n\nThe general solution to the congruence \\(14u \\equiv 46 \\pmod{100}\\) is given by \\(u = 41 + 50k\\) where \\(k\\) is an integer. The smallest positive integer solutions are \\(u = 41\\) (when \\(k = 0\\)) and \\(u = 91\\) (when \\(k = 1\\)).\n\nThe average of these two smallest positive integer solutions is \\(\\frac{41 + 91}{2} = \\frac{132}{2} = 66\\).\n\nSo, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{66}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the scale of the map and then use that scale to find the distance between the two buildings on the map.\n\nThe given scale is that 3 inches on the map corresponds to 10 miles in real life. We need to find out how many inches on the map correspond to 53.25 miles in real life.\n\nThe steps are as follows:\n\n1. Calculate the scale in inches per mile.\n2. Use the scale to find the distance on the map for 53.25 miles.\n\nLet's do the calculations step by step.\n\n1. Calculate the scale in inches per mile:\n\\[ \\text{Scale} = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{3}{10} \\text{ inches per mile} \\]\n\n2. Use the scale to find the distance on the map for 53.25 miles:\n\\[ \\text{Distance on the map} = 53.25 \\text{ miles} \\times \\frac{3}{10} \\text{ inches per mile} = \\frac{53.25 \\times 3}{10} \\text{ inches} \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values\ninches_per_10_miles = 3\nreal_life_distance = 53.25\n\n# Calculate the distance on the map\ndistance_on_map = (real_life_distance * inches_per_10_miles) / 10\nprint(distance_on_map)\n```\n```output\n15.975\n```\nThe distance between the two buildings on the map is \\(15.975\\) inches. To express this as a fraction, we note that \\(15.975\\) can be written as \\(\\frac{15975}{1000}\\). We can simplify this fraction by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 15975 and 1000.\n\nLet's find the GCD and simplify the fraction.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Numerator and denominator\nnumerator = 15975\ndenominator = 1000\n\n# Find the greatest common divisor (GCD)\ngcd = math.gcd(numerator, denominator)\n\n# Simplify the fraction\nsimplified_numerator = numerator // gcd\nsimplified_denominator = denominator // gcd\n\nsimplified_fraction = (simplified_numerator, simplified_denominator)\nprint(simplified_fraction)\n```\n```output\n(639, 40)\n```\nThe simplified fraction for \\(15.975\\) is \\(\\frac{639}{40}\\).\n\nTherefore, the distance between the two buildings on the map is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\\) inches.", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the scale of the map and then use that scale to find the distance between the two buildings on the map. The scale of the map is given as 3 inches on the map equating to 10 miles in real life. We need to find out how many inches on the map correspond to 53.25 miles in real life.\n\nHere are the steps to solve the problem:\n\n1. Calculate the scale of the map in terms of inches per mile.\n2. Use the scale to find the distance on the map that corresponds to 53.25 miles in real life.\n\nThe scale of the map is given by:\n\\[ \\text{Scale} = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{3}{10} \\text{ inches per mile} \\]\n\nTo find the distance on the map that corresponds to 53.25 miles in real life, we multiply the real-life distance by the scale:\n\\[ \\text{Distance on map} = 53.25 \\text{ miles} \\times \\frac{3}{10} \\text{ inches per mile} = \\frac{53.25 \\times 3}{10} \\text{ inches} \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values\nreal_distance = 53.25  # miles\nscale_numerator = 3  # inches\nscale_denominator = 10  # miles\n\n# Calculate the distance on 