ns are consistent with \\( S = 15 \\). Therefore, the value of \\( n \\) is \\( 7 \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{7}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure the result is accurate.\n```python\n# Define the value of n\nn = 7\n\n# Calculate the sums of the rows, columns, and diagonals\nsum_row1 = (n - 3) + 3 + (n + 1)\nsum_row2 = (n + 2) + (2 * n - 9) + 1\nsum_row3 = 2 + n + (n - 1)\nsum_col1 = (n - 3) + (n + 2) + 2\nsum_col2 = 3 + (2 * n - 9) + n\nsum_col3 = (n + 1) + 1 + (n - 1)\nsum_diag1 = (n - 3) + (2 * n - 9) + (n - 1)\nsum_diag2 = (n + 1) + (2 * n - 9) + 2\n\n# Check if all sums are equal\nS = sum_row1\nprint(((sum_row1, sum_row2, sum_row3, sum_col1, sum_col2, sum_col3, sum_diag1, sum_diag2, S)))\n```", "To solve the problem, we need to find the value of \\( n \\) such that the sum of the numbers in each row, each column, and the two main diagonals of the given magic square are equal.\n\nThe magic square is:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\n\\hline\nn-3 & 3 & n+1 \\\\\n\\hline\nn+2 & 2n-9 & 1 \\\\\n\\hline\n2 & n & n-1 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nLet's denote the common sum by \\( S \\). We can find \\( S \\) by summing the first row:\n\\[\nS = (n-3) + 3 + (n+1) = 2n - 1\n\\]\n\nNow, we can use this sum to set up equations for the other rows, columns, and diagonals. Let's start with the second row:\n\\[\n(n+2) + (2n-9) + 1 = S\n\\]\n\\[\n3n - 6 = 2n - 1\n\\]\n\\[\nn = 5\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this value of \\( n \\) by checking the other rows, columns, and diagonals. Let's substitute \\( n = 5 \\) into the magic square and check the sums:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\n\\hline\n2 & 3 & 6 \\\\\n\\hline\n7 & 1 & 1 \\\\\n\\hline\n2 & 5 & 4 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nThe sum of the first row is \\( 2 + 3 + 6 = 11 \\).\nThe sum of the second row is \\( 7 + 1 + 1 = 9 \\).\nThe sum of the third row is \\( 2 + 5 + 4 = 11 \\).\nThe sum of the first column is \\( 2 + 7 + 2 = 11 \\).\nThe sum of the second column is \\( 3 + 1 + 5