+1) + (2n-9) + 2 = S \\implies 3n - 6 = S \\]\n\nSince all these sums must be equal to \\( S \\), we can set up the equations and solve for \\( n \\). We can use the equation \\( 2n - 1 = S \\) and substitute \\( S \\) in the other equations to find \\( n \\).\n\nFrom the equations \\( 2n - 1 = S \\) and \\( 3n - 6 = S \\), we can set them equal to each other:\n\\[ 2n - 1 = 3n - 6 \\]\nSolving for \\( n \\):\n\\[ -1 + 6 = 3n - 2n \\]\n\\[ 5 = n \\]\n\nWe can verify this value by substituting \\( n = 5 \\) into the other equations to ensure consistency. Let's do this step-by-step using Python to verify the solution.\n```python\n# Define the value of n\nn = 5\n\n# Calculate the common sum S using the first row equation\nS = 2 * n - 1\n\n# Verify the sums for all rows, columns, and diagonals\nrow1_sum = (n - 3) + 3 + (n + 1)\nrow2_sum = (n + 2) + (2 * n - 9) + 1\nrow3_sum = 2 + n + (n - 1)\ncol1_sum = (n - 3) + (n + 2) + 2\ncol2_sum = 3 + (2 * n - 9) + n\ncol3_sum = (n + 1) + 1 + (n - 1)\ndiag1_sum = (n - 3) + (2 * n - 9) + (n - 1)\ndiag2_sum = (n + 1) + (2 * n - 9) + 2\n\n# Check if all sums are equal to S\nprint(((row1_sum, row2_sum, row3_sum, col1_sum, col2_sum, col3_sum, diag1_sum, diag2_sum, S)))\n```\n```output\n(9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 11, 9, 9, 9)\n```\nThe calculations show that the sums of the rows, columns, and diagonals are as follows:\n- Row 1 sum: 9\n- Row 2 sum: 9\n- Row 3 sum: 9\n- Column 1 sum: 9\n- Column 2 sum: 9\n- Column 3 sum: 11 (This should be 9, indicating an error in the initial assumption or calculation)\n- Diagonal 1 sum: 9\n- Diagonal 2 sum: 9\n\nIt appears there was an error in the initial assumption. Let's re-evaluate the equations carefully. We have:\n\\[ 2n - 1 = S \\]\n\\[ 3n - 6 = S \\]\n\\[ 2n + 1 = S \\]\n\\[ 4n - 13 = S \\]\n\\[ 3n - 6 = S \\]\n\nWe can see that the equation \\( 2n + 1 = S \\) appears twice, and it should be consistent with the other equations. Let's solve the equations again by equating \\( 2n - 1 = 3n - 6 \\) and \\( 2n +