} \\cdot \\log_b{c} = \\log_a{c}\\), we can combine the terms as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\log_2{3} \\cdot \\log_3{4} = \\log_2{4}\n\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n\\log_2{4} \\cdot \\log_4{5} \\cdot \\log_5{6} \\cdot \\log_6{7} \\cdot \\log_7{8}\n\\]\n\nNext, we can simplify \\(\\log_2{4}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\log_2{4} = \\log_2{2^2} = 2\n\\]\n\nSo the expression now is:\n\n\\[\n2 \\cdot \\log_4{5} \\cdot \\log_5{6} \\cdot \\log_6{7} \\cdot \\log_7{8}\n\\]\n\nWe can continue this process:\n\n\\[\n2 \\cdot \\log_4{5} \\cdot \\log_5{6} = 2 \\cdot \\log_4{6}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n2 \\cdot \\log_4{6} \\cdot \\log_6{7} = 2 \\cdot \\log_4{7}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n2 \\cdot \\log_4{7} \\cdot \\log_7{8} = 2 \\cdot \\log_4{8}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we simplify \\(\\log_4{8}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\log_4{8} = \\log_4{2^3} = \\log_4{4^{3/2}} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n2 \\cdot \\frac{3}{2} = 3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\log_2{3} \\cdot \\log_3{4} \\cdot \\log_4{5} \\cdot \\log_5{6} \\cdot \\log_6{7} \\cdot \\log_7{8}\\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).", "To solve the problem \\(\\log_2{3} \\cdot \\log_3{4} \\cdot \\log_4{5} \\cdot \\log_5{6} \\cdot \\log_6{7} \\cdot \\log_7{8}\\), we can use the change of base formula for logarithms. The change of base formula states that \\(\\log_a{b} = \\frac{\\log_c{b}}{\\log_c{a}}\\) for any positive base \\(c\\). By using the natural logarithm (base \\(e\\)), we can rewrite each logarithm as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\log_2{3} = \\frac{\\ln{3}}{\\ln{2}}, \\quad \\log_3{4} = \\frac{\\ln{4}}{\\ln{3}}, \\quad \\log_4{5} = \\frac{\\ln{5}}{\\ln{4}}, \\quad \\log_5{6} = \\frac{\\ln{6}}{\\ln{5}}, \\quad \\log_6{7} = \\frac{\\ln{7}}{\\ln{6}}, \\quad \\log_7{8} = \\frac{\\ln{8}}{\\ln{7}}\n\\]\n\nWhen we multiply these together, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\log_2{3} \\cdot \\log_3{4} \\cdot \\log_4{5} \\cdot \\log_5{6} \\cdot \\log_6{7} \\cdot \\log_7{8} = \\frac{\\ln{3}}{\\ln{2}} \\cdot \\frac{\\ln{4}}{\\ln{3}} \\cdot \\frac{\\ln{5}}{\\ln{4}} \\cdot \\frac{\\ln{6}}{\\ln{5}} 