ides by 0.40:\n\\[ P = \\frac{14.40}{0.40} \\]\nLet's calculate this using Python.\n```python\n# Given values\nsale_price = 14.40\ndiscount_percentage = 60\nremaining_percentage = 100 - discount_percentage\n\n# Calculate the original price\noriginal_price = sale_price / (remaining_percentage / 100)\nprint(original_price)\n```\n```output\n36.0\n```\nThe original price of the shirt was \\(\\boxed{36.00}\\) dollars.", "To find the original price of the shirt, we need to understand the relationship between the sale price and the original price. If the sale price is $60\\%$ off the original price, then the sale price is $40\\%$ of the original price. Let's denote the original price by \\( P \\). The relationship can be expressed as:\n\n\\[ \\text{Sale Price} = 0.4 \\times P \\]\n\nGiven that the sale price is $14.40, we can set up the equation:\n\n\\[ 14.40 = 0.4 \\times P \\]\n\nTo find \\( P \\), we can divide both sides of the equation by 0.4:\n\n\\[ P = \\frac{14.40}{0.4} \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given sale price and the percentage of the original price\nsale_price = 14.40\npercentage_of_original_price = 0.4\n\n# Calculate the original price\noriginal_price = sale_price / percentage_of_original_price\nprint(original_price)\n```\n```output\n36.0\n```\nThe original price of the shirt was \\(\\boxed{36.00}\\) dollars.", "To determine the original price of the shirt, let's denote the original price by \\( P \\). The sale price is given as $14.40, which is 60% off the original price. This means that the sale price is 40% of the original price (since 100% - 60% = 40%).\n\nSo, we can write the equation:\n\\[ 0.4 \\times P = 14.40 \\]\n\nTo find \\( P \\), we can solve the equation by dividing both sides by 0.4:\n\\[ P = \\frac{14.40}{0.4} \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given sale price and discount percentage\nsale_price = 14.40\ndiscount_percentage = 60\n\n# Calculate the original