   ]\r\n    \r\n    min_sum_abs = float('inf')\r\n    for factors in factorizations:\r\n        current_sum_abs = abs(sum(factors))\r\n        if current_sum_abs < min_sum_abs:\r\n            min_sum_abs = current_sum_abs\r\n    \r\n    return 2 * min_sum_abs\r\n\r\n# Calculate the minimum absolute value of a_{n-1}\r\nmin_abs_a_n_minus_1_value = min_abs_a_n_minus_1()\r\nprint(min_abs_a_n_minus_1_value)\n```\n```output\n30\n```\nThe least possible value of \\(|a_{n-1}|\\) is \\(\\boxed{30}\\).", "To determine the total number of different personalities Tom can create for his Mr. Potato Head, we need to consider each of the components that make up the personality: eyebrows, eyes, ears, lips, shoes, and optionally hair. Each of these components can be chosen independently of the others.\n\nHere's the breakdown of the components and their respective choices:\n- eyebrows: 2 sets (left and right)\n- eyes: 1 pair\n- ears: 2 sets (left and right)\n- lips: 2 sets\n- shoes: 2 pairs (regular and clown shoes)\n- hair: 3 hairstyles (including bald)\n\nSince each component can be chosen independently, the total number of different personalities is the product of the number of choices for each component. The calculation is as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total number of personalities} = (\\text{number of eyebrow choices}) \\times (\\text{number of eye choices}) \\times (\\text{number of ear choices}) \\times (\\text{number of lip choices}) \\times (\\text{number of shoe choices}) \\times (\\text{number of hair choices})\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total number of personalities} = 2 \\times 1 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 3\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Number of choices for each component\neyebrow_choices = 2\neye_choices = 1\near_choices = 2\nlip_choices = 2\nshoe_choices = 2\nhair_choices = 3\n\n# Total number of different personalities\ntotal_personalities = eyebrow_choices * eye_choices * ear_choices * lip_choices * shoe_choices * hair_